{
  "version": 1,
  "_about": [
    "Income/amount vocabulary for the reach layer, as DATA rather than hand-written",
    "regex escapes in Python source. Adding a language (or a new way of writing",
    "lakh/crore/thousand) is a JSON edit here plus a test run — no raw \\uXXXX",
    "sequences to mistype. tests/test_numerals.py fails if a supported language is",
    "missing a multiplier, and if a glyph is in the wrong Unicode block (the class",
    "of bug that once put a Devanagari letter in the Bengali table).",
    "Words are matched longest-first with Unicode word boundaries."
  ],
